+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-goal-completion-gate
+
+An independent completion gate for `update_goal`. `dsh-tool-goal` marks a
+goal complete on the model's own word; this plugin denies the call unless the
+assistant narration that carries it cites session-verifiable evidence.
+
+## Behavior
+
+A `tools/pre-execute` hook intercepts `update_goal` calls whose `action` is
+`complete` (other actions stay transparent). The gate extracts citation
+candidates from the assistant message carrying the call — backtick spans,
+quoted spans, and path- or identifier-like tokens — and verifies each against
+the session log's anchor corpus: recent tool call ids, call arguments, and
+result texts. With fewer than `minVerifiedCitations` verified citations the
+call is denied with corrective feedback naming exactly what is required, so
+the model retries with citations instead of failing the turn. Calls without
+an owning agent (direct `ctx.tools.execute()`) are not gated.
+
+The gate adds one system-prompt policy section while loaded so the model
+learns the requirement before the first denial. It changes no tool schema and
+composes with `dsh-tool-goal` and `dsh-goal-progress-guard` unmodified; it is
+not part of shipped default profiles.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Field | Default | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `goalToolName` | `'update_goal'` | Name of the goal-update tool whose `complete` action is gated. |
+| `minVerifiedCitations` | `1` | Verified citations required to admit a completion. |
+| `anchorEventWindow` | `400` | Recent session events scanned for verifiable anchors. |
+| `minCitationLength` | `6` | Minimum character length for a citation candidate. |
+
+Misconfiguration throws at plugin load. Opt in through a profile overlay:
+
+```yaml
+plugins:
+  - id: goal-completion-gate
+    name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-goal-completion-gate'
+```
+
+## Model Experience
+
+One short system-prompt section while loaded; one corrective tool-error
+result per denied completion. No history rewriting, no token-budget impact
+beyond those two bounded texts.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- Verification is verbatim substring matching against the anchor corpus. It
+  proves the cited artifact exists in the session, not that it proves the
+  objective — semantic adequacy of evidence is deferred to the L2/L3 gate
+  tiers (an executable acceptance check, or an independent verifier
+  subagent).
+- Citations are read from the latest assistant message only; a model that
+  separates its evidence narration from the `update_goal` call by further
+  tool calls must repeat the citation in the carrying message.
+- Fabricated tool call ids are not distinguished from other unverifiable
+  citations; both are denied identically.
+- This package omits `./invariant`: the gated-denial relation is asserted
+  directly by the behavior suite, and there is no second independent
+  observation to diverge.
